  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Mitigation and Preparedness in Action (Impact) - Republic of the Marshall Islands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The increasing intensity of extreme weather disturbances and hazards in the Republic of the Marshall Islands (RMI) requires greater investment in disaster risk reduction and mitigation efforts. The Inclusive Mitigation and Preparedness in Action (IMPACT) project contributes to the overall enhancement of capacity within communities and governments to be better prepared for, and more resilient to hazard events and disasters. The project seeks to equip communities with the resources and skills to actively mitigate hazards; prioritize an inclusive approach with traditionally underrepresented populations; and support response planning through joint damage assessments. Community-ownership and government buy-in are critical to sustaining achievements under the project, and IOM works in close coordination with the National Disaster Management Office throughout the project. Furthermore, the project emphasizes multiple visits to the select communities for monitoring purposes and to strengthen the interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
